      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Room-temperature χMT = 55.52 cm3 K mol−1 (expected 56.68 for four isolated Dy(III)). χMT decreases on cooling then rises below 10 K, attributed to depopulation of mJ states and/or antiferromagnetic exchange plus ferromagnetic dipolar interactions. Zero-field out-of-phase ac susceptibility appears only at high frequency; field-induced SMM behavior with two relaxation channels under 2000 Oe. LF: minor Orbach (τ0 = 4.43(7)×10−16 s, Ueff = 160.9(84) K) plus dominant direct process; HF: Raman + direct. Demonstrated field-induced single-molecule magnet behavior.",
        "measurements": [
